sm","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL40085272M/Yoga_in_Modern_Hinduism","details":{"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL7912034A","name":"Knut A. Jacobsen"}],"isbn_13":["9781315113340"],"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"pagination":"234","publish_date":"2017","publishers":["Taylor & Francis Group"],"source_records":["bwb:9781315113340"],"title":"Yoga in Modern Hinduism","subtitle":"Hariharānanda Āraṇya and Sāṃkhyayoga","full_title":"Yoga in Modern Hinduism Hariharānanda Āraṇya and Sāṃkhyayoga","works":[{"key":"/works/OL22146821W"}],"key":"/books/OL40085272M","latest_revision":2,"revision":2,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2022-10-19T10:34:50.153556"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2026-06-11T01:06:06.402301"}}},"ISBN:9781138080591":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9781138080591","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL34643857M/Yoga_in_Modern_Hinduism","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL34643857M/Yoga_in_Modern_Hinduism","details":{"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL7912034A","name":"Knut A. Jacobsen"}],"isbn_13":["9781138080591"],"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"lc_classifications":["B132.S3J33 2017","B132.S3 J33 2018"],"publish_date":"2017","publishers":["Taylor & Francis Group"],"source_records":["bwb:9781138080591","marc:marc_columbia/Columbia-extract-20221130-031.mrc:242162914:4776","marc:harvard_bibliographic_metadata/20220215_026.bib.mrc:50929978:3482"],"subjects":["Sankhya"],"title":"Yoga in Modern Hinduism","weight":"0.455","pagination":"234","subtitle":"Hariharānanda Āraṇya and Sāṃkhyayoga","full_title":"Yoga in Modern Hinduism Hariharānanda Āraṇya and Sāṃkhyayoga","works":[{"key":"/works/OL22146821W"}],"key":"/books/OL34643857M","oclc_numbers":["1016382575","1010700688"],"lccn":["2017038459"],"description":{"type":"/type/text","value":"The Samkhyayoga institution of Kapil Math is a religious organisation with a small tradition of followers which emerged in the last decade of the nineteenth century and the first decades of the twentieth century in Bengal in India around the renunciant and yogin Hariharananda Aranya. This tradition developed during the same period in which modern yoga was born and forms a chapter in the expansion of yoga traditions in modern Hinduism. The book analyses the yoga teaching of Hariharananda Aranya (1869-1947) and the Kapil Math tradition, its origin, history and contemporary manifestations, and this tradition's connection to the expansion of yoga and the Yogasutra in modern Hinduism. The Samkhyayoga of the Kapil Math tradition is based on the Patanjalayogasastra, on a number of texts in Sanskrit and Bengali written by their gurus, and on the lifestyle of the renunciant yogin living isolated in a cave. The book investigates Hariharananda Aranya's connection to pre-modern yoga traditions and the impact of modern production and transmission of knowledge on his interpretations of yoga. The book connects the Kapil Math tradition to the nineteenth century transformations of Bengali religious culture of the educated upper class that led to the production of a new type of yogin. The book analyses Samkhyayoga as a living tradition, its current teachings and practices, and looks at what Samkhyayogins do and what Samkhyayoga is as a yoga practice."},"number_of_pages":234,"latest_revision":4,"revision":4,"created":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2021-10-06T19:26:02.502879"},"last_modified":{"type":"/type/datetime","value":"2026-06-11T00:57:01.856645"}}},"ISBN:9781000041620":{"bib_key":"ISBN:9781000041620","info_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL33783713M/Yogasūtra_of_Patañjali","preview":"noview","preview_url":"http://openlibrary.org/books/OL33783713M/Yogasūtra_of_Patañjali","details":{"type":{"key":"/type/edition"},"authors":[{"key":"/authors/OL3647185A","name":"Pradeep P. Gokhale"}],"isbn_13":["9781000041620"],"languages":[{"key":"/languages/eng"}],"num